From: HempFiend <17104973+jaidenscool1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 03:05:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 07/10] NAT discovery answers the open-NAT test; matchmaking
 drops a host's sessions on disconnect

stun: mode 3 is answered from the second server's IP on port+1 (read from the
client's NAT type logic), so titles report an open NAT; requests are logged.
matchmaking: sessions remember the connection that created them and are
removed when it closes, so searches don't return dead hosts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
